    {
      "id": "a0748b750832179d4d4532dcdb94b7b1e8b91f77",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1322208567,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The lapdm_data_t was introduced in commit 9097d1b07c2f03badf9c39f8b338b1dcbb55f18e to pass meta-data from the calling dissector into the LAPDm dissector.  That may be insufficient/buggy, so it might need fixing/estension.\n\nHowever, it looks like your removal of the lapdm_data_t makes that obsolete? I am really lacking the time for a thorough analysis right now, but it seems more logical to me to keep passing the lapdm_data_t between dissectors - and if needed extend/expand that.\n\nIn general, the LAPDm dissector shouldn't make assumptions on who is calling it (gsmtap is only one of multiple already existing callers), so passing a gsmtap-protocol-value into the LAPDm dissector looks like it's violating the layer separation here.",
          "author": {
            "id": 357252,
            "username": "laf0rge",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Harald Welte",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
